Wyoming Department of Health, Aging Division
FY 2017 Title III-B Grant Application
Competitive Grant Application Program Goals
Grantee:
City of Cheyenne (Transit Program)
Mission and Goals of 2017TitleIII-B Supportive Services Program
Mission and Goals of 2017TitleIII-B Supportive Services Program
Title III-B Program enables older individuals, 60 and older, to remain physical, mental and social active through
ownhomes by providing supportive services, to enhance their health and tobe active contributors to their
families and communities.
Scope of the Program-The provision of any or all TitleII-B services as described in Section 321 of the Older
Americans Act; with emphasis on identifying and serving low income, rural, minority and limited English
proficient older individuals.These services may include Health Services, Socialization, Support Services
including Information &Assistance, and Transportation and a widevariety of other supportive services that
enrich and stabilize the lives of seniors.
Listed below are the allowable services and/or activities within the Health Services category.In the green box
below each service, you must select:"YES"for the services that WILL be provided, and select"NO" for the
services that WILL NOT be provided.Every shaded boxMUST be marked "YES"if you answered "YES"
in the green box for this service category.
A.Health Services(including mental health)
NO this service will NOT be provided
Individual clients will improve healthby increasing participation in health activities.Example:
Health Education Class, Health Exercise and Preventive Health check/Screening Services.
